l theme episode 9 could feature a  sequence in which a ghostly Vader is  providing counsel to kylo Ren secretly  guiding him toward a decisive loss at  the hands of the resistance only for Ren  to learn the ghost is actually the force  ghost of Luke Skywalker tricking kylo to  help his friends if nothing else it  would be a suitable follow-up to Luke's  promise that he'll see kylo again  the end of the last Jedi in the force  awakens Rey experiences what would later  be termed a force back in which our  contact with Luke's lightsaber gives her  a glimpse of both the past and future of  the Star Wars saga that lightsaber was  Luke's and his father's before him and  now he calls to you filled with  references to Star Wars past and present  this sequence has provided fertile  ground for Star Wars fans speculators a  flashback in episode 9 would offer  another easy way for Abrams to introduce  Darth Vader back into the saga kylo  could get a glimpse of a pivotal moment  in Bader's life through contact with his  helmet or another character could  remember their own encounter with Vader  from the past one piece of old universe  lore that has been reintroduced is the  holocron a small device usually a cube  that can hold training and insights from  either Jedi or Sith when the holocron is  activated the recording is played back  as a hologram similar to Princess Leia  projecting from r2d2 in the original  Star Wars the holocron was introduced in  1991 in the dark empire comic series and  returned to modern continuity in later  comics and the Clone Wars and rebels  television series it's a handy plot  device whether as a MacGuffin to prompt  a Jedi or Sith race across the galaxy or  an easy way to cram in some exposition  through the broadcast of a long-lost  character more interestingly if Vader  recorded his own holocron of sith  insights it's possible kylo Ren might  have discovered it and could replay it  in episode 9 in Revenge of the Sith  Palpatine explains the anakin that dark  Plagueis was a Sith Lord obsessed with  immortality who mastered the ability to  create life through the manipulation of  midi-chlorians Plagueis was once Darth  Sidious Sith master and as soon as  Sidious mastered his own grasp of this  arcane art he murdered Plagueis in his  sleep a single panel in the fortress  Vader storyline from the Darth Vader  comic series connects this Sith legend  to one of the biggest questions in Star  Wars lore the parentage of Anakin  Skywalker we know Anakin's mother wish  me a slave from Tatooine but his father  has always remained a mystery  invaders journey through Mustafa's  mysterious darkside portal he has a  vision of his mother as Palpatine lurks  just over her shoulder manipulating  strange  energies in her womb it's the closest  star wars has come to implying that the  father of Anakin Skywalker is in fact  Emperor Palpatine using the powers he  learned from Darth Plagueis to create  life it's possible this knowledge didn't  die with Palpatine and then he passed it  on somehow either to his apprentice or  with a holocron or other vessel kylos  discovery of such knowledge would set  him on the path to mastering it and  resurrecting his grandfather it's very  clear that episode 9s filmmakers could  bring back Vader if they wanted to but  should they it's a tough question on one  hand this new Star Wars trilogy has  managed to cleverly fold in elements of  the past films and surprising and  resonant ways if they do bring back  Darth Vader it's sure to feel  significant and creatively fulfilling  and if you viewed the total nine film  story of the main line Star Wars films  as the saga of the Skywalker family then  it would make sense for the patriarch to  return one last time and influence the  events surrounding his grandsons rise to  power on the other hand Vader has become  iconic partly because when he does  appear it truly matters take that  sequence in rogue one sure it was a nice  excuse for an extended sequence of Sith  badassery using all of the special  effects and filmmaking skills the crew  had to offer but it was also a  demonstration of Bader's impact on a  moment of key importance to the entire  Star Wars galaxy if he had succeeded the  Death Star plans would have remained in  the Empire's possession and the  burgeoning rebellion might have been  snuffed out his failure had immense  consequences for the story as a whole  ultimately that's the real question fans  should be asking about Darth Vader in  the run-up to episode 9 not whether he  can return to the story but instead what  kind of monumental events could warrant  his reappearance in a galaxy far far  away check out one of our newest videos  right here plus even more looper videos  about Star Wars are coming soon  subscribe to our YouTube channel and hit  the bell so you don't miss a single one  [Music]
 

